oncurrency safety of `req.WithContext` and `req.Context()`.\\n\\nOnce these components introduce certain mechanisms for concurrency safety, it may lead to performance degradation.\\n\\nFor users pursuing high performance, such performance degradation is unacceptable. Moreover, once implemented, users have no choice but to use these mechanisms.\\n\\nTherefore, I prefer to leave the decision of whether to ensure concurrency safety to the users themselves, and let them implement these mechanisms on their own.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston discuss 27 linux foundat easycla bot 2025 10 14t04 01 31z a href http easycla lfx linuxfound org version 2 img src http s3 amazonaw com cla project logo prod cla sign svg v2 alt cla sign align left height 28 width 328 a br br the committ list abov are author under a sign cla ul li white _ check _ mark login nicksherron name nick sherron 43d6c1b5f0c27c73a83543d0f681e2dc766d86dc 6c560fe0a618c400f5961126b3daf71074a98113 ebe29b975966edee33e7c0e2fdcca7c89710fd63 li ul flc1125 2025 10 14t04 35 20z the current chang do not guarante thread safeti addit i lean toward the view that for infrastructur level compon or framework there is no need to consid the concurr safeti of req withcontext and req context onc these compon introduc certain mechan for concurr safeti it may lead to perform degrad for user pursu high perform such perform degrad is unaccept moreov onc implement user have no choic but to use these mechan therefor i prefer to leav the decis of whether to ensur concurr safeti to the user themselv and let them implement these mechan on their own\"