row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.37009640393507015, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.18229347419295747, \"vector_similarity\": 0.80830324, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874bc7c88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 2849, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 1120, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-05]\\n\\n# Issue: otelconf: add support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE variable (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8059)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8059  \\n\\n**Author**: codeboten  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-22T21:25:29Z · **Updated**: 2026-04-03T11:34:34Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: enhancement, area: file-config  \\n\\n**Milestone**: untracked\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n### Component\\n\\nConfig\\n\\n### Problem Statement\\n\\nAs per the spec:\\n\\n> Setting the [OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/configuration/sdk-environment-variables.md#declarative-configuration) environment variable (for languages that support it) provides users a convenient way to initialize OpenTelemetry components without needing to learn language-specific configuration details or use a large number of environment variables. The pattern for accessing the configured components and installing into instrumentation will vary by language. For example, the usage in Java might resemble:\\n\\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/configuration/sdk.md#via-otel_experimental_config_file\\n\\n### Proposed Solution\\n\\nOpen to suggestions of how this should be implemented to align w/ the rest of the Go SDK implementation\\n\\n### Alternatives\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Prior Art\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional Context\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-05]\\n\\n# Issue: otelconf: add support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE variable (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8059)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8059  \\n\\n**Author**: codeboten  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-22T21:25:29Z · **Updated**: 2026-04-03T11:34:34Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: enhancement, area: file-config  \\n\\n**Milestone**: untracked\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Discussion (2)\\n\\n**codeboten** — 2025-10-23T17:18:25Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src issu 05 issu otelconf add support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file variabl open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8059 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8059 author codeboten creat 2025 10 22t21 25 29z updat 2026 04 03t11 34 34z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label enhanc area file config mileston untrack descript compon config problem statement a per the spec set the otel _ experiment _ config _ file http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif blob main specif configur sdk environ variabl md declar configur environ variabl for languag that support it provid user a conveni way to initi opentelemetri compon without need to learn languag specif configur detail or use a larg number of environ variabl the pattern for access the configur compon and instal into instrument will vari by languag for exampl the usag in java might resembl http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif blob main specif configur sdk md via otel _ experiment _ config _ file propos solut open to suggest of how this should be implement to align w the rest of the go sdk implement altern _ no respons _ prior art _ no respons _ addit context _ no respons _ sourc id src issu 05 issu otelconf add support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file variabl open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8059 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8059 author codeboten creat 2025 10 22t21 25 29z updat 2026 04 03t11 34 34z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label enhanc area file config mileston untrack discuss 2 codeboten 2025 10 23t17 18 25z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874bc7c88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"id\": \"d162a2a65d87b225\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.35361363445171545, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.16393719207387927, \"vector_similarity\": 0.796192, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874bc7c88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 2849, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 1120, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-05]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479626706  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-23\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Alex Boten\\n\\n- David Ashpole (dashpole)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n### PR status: JSON/YAML unmarshalling\\n\\n- A small change (error tag) was suggested and applied.\\n\\n- Build is running; plan is to merge once green.\\n\\n### Adding env var support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE\\n\\nReference: Adding env var support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8059\\n\\n- Goal:\\n\\n  - If the env var is present, load the indicated config file and configure the SDK automatically, minimizing user code.\\n\\n- Current ecosystem notes:\\n\\n  - PHP reports support; other languages vary (JS likely working on it; C++ explicitly not supporting).\\n\\n  - Go users are accustomed to programmatic setup; unclear if SDK-level support is necessary.\\n\\n- Go implementation options discussed:\\n\\n  - SDK experimental feature-flag approach:\\n\\n    - Use internal “x”/experimental packages to expose a feature gate for the env var.\\n\\n    - Check the env var during SDK setup (e.g., TracerProvider construction), and if enabled, configure from the file.\\n\\n    - Complications:\\n\\n      - Potential import cycles (e.g., if otelconf needs sdk and vice versa).\\n\\n      - Decision required on how to handle passed options vs. config file (ignore vs. merge).\\n\\n      - Requires similar work across trace, metrics, and logs modules.\\n\\n  - Contrib-first approach (preferred short term):\\n\\n    - Implement in opentelemetry-go-contrib/otelconf:\\n\\n      - Provide an explicit function to load from OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE and construct/return SDK providers.\\n\\n      - Optionally offer an init-based side effect that sets the global provider if the env var is set (not ideal, but acceptable during experimental phase to collect feedback).\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 05 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479626706 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z updat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 23 attende tyler yahn alex boten david ashpol dashpol transcript pr status json yaml unmarshal a small chang error tag wa suggest and appli build is run plan is to merg onc green ad env var support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file refer ad env var support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8059 goal if the env var is present load the indic config file and configur the sdk automat minim user code current ecosystem note php report support other languag vari j like work on it c explicit not support go user are accustom to programmat setup unclear if sdk level support is necessari go implement option discuss sdk experiment featur flag approach use intern x experiment packag to expos a featur gate for the env var check the env var dure sdk setup e g tracerprovid construct and if enabl configur from the file complic potenti import cycl e g if otelconf need sdk and vice versa decis requir on how to handl pass option v config file ignor v merg requir similar work across trace metric and log modul contrib first approach prefer short term implement in opentelemetri go contrib otelconf provid an explicit function to load from otel _ experiment _ config _ file and construct return sdk provid option offer an init base side effect that set the global provid if the env var is set not ideal but accept dure experiment phase to collect feedback\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"873abbfe8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"id\": \"1fe86388dce9138e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.311604775686067, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1290831366943814, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7374886, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"873abbfe8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4412, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:29\", \"token_count\": 1155, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-04]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Use sync.Map and atomics to improve sum performance (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go#7427)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7427  \\n\\n**Author**: dashpole  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-09-29T14:36:56Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-14T14:40:27Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: merged (2025-10-07T13:40:23Z)  \\n\\n**Branch**: `optimize_counter_syncmap` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +437 / -121 across 14 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: area:metrics  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.39.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Review Comments (18)\\n\\n**MrAlias** on `CHANGELOG.md` — 2025-10-02T17:55:27Z\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n- Improve performance of concurrent measurements in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric`. (#7427)\\n\\n```\\n\\n**MrAlias** on `sdk/metric/internal/aggregate/aggregate.go` — 2025-10-03T00:03:10Z\\n\\nPassing the temporality only to then parse it below and make a decision here seems like a bad smell. I'm more inclined to refactoring the Sum in some way to better address this and remove the control param being passed here.\\n\\n**MrAlias** on `sdk/metric/internal/aggregate/sum.go` — 2025-10-03T15:10:13Z\\n\\nA pre-increment approach with rollback may address this.\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n\\t\\t// Pre-increment, reserve a slot first.\\n\\n\\t\\tnewLen := s.len[hotIdx].Add(1)\\n\\n\\t\\tif s.aggLimit > 0 && newLen >= int64(s.aggLimit) {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t// We exceeded the limit, decrement back and use overflow\\n\\n\\t\\t\\ts.len[hotIdx].Add(-1)\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tfltrAttr = overflowSet\\n\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\n```\\n\\n**MrAlias** on `sdk/metric/internal/aggregate/sum.go` — 2025-10-03T15:14:24Z\\n\\nSplitting this into a type dedicated to cumulative values seems appropriate. It would have fields like this right?\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 04 pull request use sync map and atom to improv sum perform open telemetri opentelemetri go 7427 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7427 author dashpol creat 2025 09 29t14 36 56z updat 2025 10 14t14 40 27z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 10 07t13 40 23z branch optim _ counter _ syncmap main chang 437 121 across 14 file label area metric mileston v1 39 0 review comment 18 mralia on changelog md 2025 10 02t17 55 27z suggest improv perform of concurr measur in go opentelemetri io otel sdk metric 7427 mralia on sdk metric intern aggreg aggreg go 2025 10 03t00 03 10z pass the tempor onli to then pars it below and make a decis here seem like a bad smell i m more inclin to refactor the sum in some way to better address this and remov the control param be pass here mralia on sdk metric intern aggreg sum go 2025 10 03t15 10 13z a pre increment approach with rollback may address this suggest pre increment reserv a slot first newlen s len hotidx add 1 if s agglimit 0 newlen int64 s agglimit we exceed the limit decrement back and use overflow s len hotidx add 1 fltrattr overflowset mralia on sdk metric intern aggreg sum go 2025 10 03t15 14 24z split this into a type dedic to cumul valu seem appropri it would have field like this right suggest\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875c049e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"id\": \"4b83ef940640c267\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3043304478703166, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1298929226718809, \"vector_similarity\": 0.71135134, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875c049e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 37741, \"chunk_count\": 26, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:02\", \"token_count\": 14705, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"* chore(deps): update module go.uber.org/zap to v1.27.1 by @renovate[bot] in https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7620\\n\\n* chore(deps): update module github.com/cyphar/filepath-securejoin to v0.6.1 by @renovate[bot] in https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7618\\n\\n* chore(deps): update module golang.org/x/crypto to v0.45.0 [security] by @renovate[bot] in https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7622\\n\\n* chore(deps): update actions/checkout action to v6 by @renovate[bot] in https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7624\\n\\n* otlploghttp: support OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_LOGS_INSECURE and OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_INSECURE env vars by @fd in https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7608\\n\\n* chore(deps): update module dev.gaijin.team/go/golib to v0.8.0 by @renovate[bot] in https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7627\