go pull 7629 chore dep updat github codeql action action to v4 315 by renov bot in http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7631 chore dep updat modul github com tomarrel wrapcheck v2 to v2 120 by renov bot in http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7632\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8765f6c08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"id\": \"ab7f0fa6b8d4b962\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3007611994101278, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11905233487161113, \"vector_similarity\": 0.72474855, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8765f6c08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 52878, \"chunk_count\": 30, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:56\", \"token_count\": 15994, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I would lean towards the solution proposed by the SIG: only support configurability when users explicitly request it. After all, enabling configurability after `RemoveAll()` is an operation that ensures both extensibility compatibility and backward compatibility.\\n\\n@akats7 @dmathieu \\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-11-10T02:01:52Z\\n\\nAh gotcha, didn't see that that was mentioned. I'm good on holding off until it's explicitly requested.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-11-10T04:27:26Z\\n\\n@Yiling-J I think we're good to resolve the conflicts and close this out, thanks!\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-11-10T11:58:48Z\\n\\nI’ve resolved the conflicts, and the otelgin package tests passed on my machine @flc1125 @dmathieu @akats7 \\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-11-10T14:02:53Z\\n\\nCould you add the corresponding unit tests for this scenario?\\n\\n> My only concern with RemoveAll is on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-11-10T15:21:14Z\\n\\n> Could you add the corresponding unit tests for this scenario?\\n\\n> \\n\\n> > My only concern with RemoveAll is on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data.\\n\\nI’ve added more details to the test case, it now includes two extra middlewares, one upstream and one downstream, to demonstrate what happens when `RemoveAll` is called in the otel middleware. The behavior is correct to me, but let’s confirm that we all agree it’s the expected one.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609  \\n\\n**Author**: Yiling-J  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-01-13T13:45:43Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-13T01:26:12Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/gin_multipartform` → `main`  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i would lean toward the solut propos by the sig onli support configur when user explicit request it after all enabl configur after removeal is an oper that ensur both extens compat and backward compat akats7 dmathieu akats7 2025 11 10t02 01 52z ah gotcha didn t see that that wa mention i m good on hold off until it s explicit request akats7 2025 11 10t04 27 26z yile j i think we re good to resolv the conflict and close this out thank yile j 2025 11 10t11 58 48z i ve resolv the conflict and the otelgin packag test pass on my machin flc1125 dmathieu akats7 flc1125 2025 11 10t14 02 53z could you add the correspond unit test for this scenario my onli concern with removeal is on the off chanc that a middlewar further up the chain still expect access to the form data yile j 2025 11 10t15 21 14z could you add the correspond unit test for this scenario my onli concern with removeal is on the off chanc that a middlewar further up the chain still expect access to the form data i ve ad more detail to the test case it now includ two extra middlewar one upstream and one downstream to demonstr what happen when removeal is call in the otel middlewar the behavior is correct to me but let s confirm that we all agre it s the expect one sourc id src pr 01 pull request fix otelgin remov multipartform temporari file open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 6609 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 author yile j creat 2025 01 13t13 45 43z updat 2025 11 13t01 26 12z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open branch fix gin _ multipartform main\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"8a1254612e6e6337\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29955685479608024, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10375238113725752, \"vector_similarity\": 0.75643396, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-04]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Use sync.Map and atomics to improve sum performance (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go#7427)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7427  \\n\\n**Author**: dashpole  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-09-29T14:36:56Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-14T14:40:27Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: merged (2025-10-07T13:40:23Z)  \\n\\n**Branch**: `optimize_counter_syncmap` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +437 / -121 across 14 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: area:metrics  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.39.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAlternative to https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7380\\n\\nThis uses a sync.Map and atomics for the sum's counter value.  This intentionally introduces a new race condition that didn't previously exist:\\n\\n* It is possible for the exemplar to be recorded in the batch of metrics after the add() for cumulative sum aggregations. For cumulative, this isn't a huge issue since exemplars are expected to persist across collection cycles. This is difficult to fix because we can't manage the internal storage of an exemplar.Reservoir (to atomically swap between hot and cold storage).  If we are able to make assumptions about how exemplar reservoirs are managed (i.e. that the number of and order of exemplars returned is always the same), then we could possibly fix this by merging at export time.\\n\\n### Alternatives Considered\\n\\n#### RWLock for the map instead of sync.Map\\n\\nThis is significantly less performant.\\n\\n#### Single sync.Map without hotColdWaitGroup\\n\\nDeleting keys from the sync.Map concurrently with measurements (during Clear() of the sync.Map) can cause measurements to be made to a counter that has already been read, exported and deleted.  This can produce incorrect sums when delta is used.  Instead, atomically switching writes to a completely empty sync.Map and waiting for writes to the previous sync.Map complete eliminates this issue.\\n\\n#### Use two sync.Map for cumulative sums\\n\\nOne idea I explored was doing a hot-cold swap for cumulative sums just like we do for delta sums.  We would swap the hot and cold sync.Maps, wait for writes to the cold sync.Map to complete while new writes go to the hot map.  Then, once we are done reading the cold map, we could merge the contents of the cold map back into the new hot map.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 04 pull request use sync map and atom to improv sum perform open telemetri opentelemetri go 7427 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7427 author dashpol creat 2025 09 29t14 36 56z updat 2025 10 14t14 40 27z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 10 07t13 40 23z branch optim _ counter _ syncmap main chang 437 121 across 14 file label area metric mileston v1 39 0 descript altern to http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7380 this us a sync map and atom for the sum s counter valu this intent introduc a new race condit that didn t previous exist it is possibl for the exemplar to be record in the batch of metric after the add for cumul sum aggreg for cumul this isn t a huge issu sinc exemplar are expect to persist across collect cycl this is difficult to fix becaus we can t manag the intern storag of an exemplar reservoir to atom swap between hot and cold storag if we are abl to make assumpt about how exemplar reservoir are manag i e that the number of and order of exemplar return is alway the same then we could possibl fix this by merg at export time altern consid rwlock for the map instead of sync map this is signific less perform singl sync map without hotcoldwaitgroup delet key from the sync map concurr with measur dure clear of the sync map can caus measur to be made to a counter that ha alreadi been read export and delet this can produc incorrect sum when delta is use instead atom switch write to a complet empti sync map and wait for write to the previous sync map complet elimin this issu use two sync map for cumul sum one idea i explor wa do a hot cold swap for cumul sum just like we do for delta sum we would swap the hot and cold sync map wait for write to the cold sync map to complet while new write go to the hot map then onc we are done read the cold map we could merg the content of the cold map back into the new hot map\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875c049e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"id\": \"48f382952d1f96ae\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29928205617890447, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12117940882700642, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7148549, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875c049e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 37741, \"chunk_count\": 26, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:02\", \"token_count\": 14705, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-05]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Optimize histogram reservoir (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go#7443)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7443  \\n\\n**Author**: dashpole  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-02T13:56:40Z · **Updated**: 2025-12-15T15:00:11Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: merged (2025-12-15T14:59:34Z)  \\n\\n**Branch**: `optimize_histogram_reservoir` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +173 / -61 across 8 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.40.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThis improves the concurrent performance of the histogram reservoir's Offer function by 4x (i.e. 75% reduction).\\n\\nAccomplish this by locking each measurement, rather than locking around the entire storage.  Also, defer extracting the trace context from context.Context until collection time. This improves the performance of Offer, which is on the measure hot path.  Exemplars are often overwritten, so deferring the operation until Collect reduces the overall work.\\n\\n```\\n\\n                           │   main.txt   │              hist.txt              │\\n\\n                           │    sec/op    │   sec/op     vs base               │\\n\\nFixedSizeReservoirOffer-24    211.4n ± 3%   177.5n ± 3%  -16.04% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\nHistogramReservoirOffer-24   200.85n ± 2%   47.41n ± 2%  -76.40% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\ngeomean                       206.1n        91.73n       -55.48%\\n\\n```\\n\\nBenchmarks for Measure:\\n\\n```\\n\\n                                                                                 │  main.txt   │             histres.txt             │\\n\\n                                                                                 │   sec/op    │    sec/op     vs base               │\\n\\nSyncMeasure/NoView/ExemplarsEnabled/Int64Histogram/Attributes/0-24                 436.7n ± 4%   114.8n ±  5%  -73.72% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\nSyncMeasure/NoView/ExemplarsEnabled/Int64Histogram/Attributes/10-24                472.2n ± 2%   169.7n ±  8%  -64.08% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 05 pull request optim histogram reservoir open telemetri opentelemetri go 7443 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7443 author dashpol creat 2025 10 02t13 56 40z updat 2025 12 15t15 00 11z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 12 15t14 59 34z branch optim _ histogram _ reservoir main chang 173 61 across 8 file label mileston v1