github com open telemetri opentelemetri go and http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib relat http github com integr terraform provid github issu 2746 trask is it a blocker trask 2025 11 07t00 20 03z trask is it a blocker it doesn t need to block let s do someth like this http github com open telemetri admin pull 346 pellar 2025 12 11t17 43 19z i can confirm that it work for go http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go releas tag v1 39 0 and go contrib http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib releas tag v1 39 0\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874919b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"id\": \"85135205c17775f5\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3454049363476348, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.19121489478233542, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7051817, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874919b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 6168, \"chunk_count\": 5, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:19\", \"token_count\": 2203, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-06]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479655348  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:39:04Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:40:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-30\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Bryan Boreham\\n\\n- Damien Mathieu\\n\\n- Robert Pająk\\n\\n- David Ashpole\\n\\n- Mike Blum\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n### Monitoring bugs reported by OSS-Fuzz\\n\\n- David proposed enabling automatic filing of OSS-Fuzz findings as GitHub issues to track and triage them in-repo.\\n\\n- Robert noted OSS-Fuzz runs in Google CI; access and notifications currently limited. Some maintainers may need to be added as contacts.\\n\\n- Tyler and David highlighted that OSS-Fuzz does not file public issues by default due to potential security sensitivity of fuzz findings.\\n\\n- Consensus:\\n\\n  - Start by setting up a maintainers mailing list for OSS-Fuzz notifications (via GC) and trial monitoring for a few months.\\n\\n  - Avoid enabling public GitHub issue filing for now; reassess after triage/verification workflows are in place.\\n\\n  - Robert can manually recreate older issues if needed.\\n\\n- Bryan shared Prometheus project’s recent discussion comparing OSS-Fuzz with Go’s built-in fuzzing; Robert emphasized OSS-Fuzz’s continuous background fuzzing as a benefit.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- [Monitoring bugs reported by OSS Fuzz #7549](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/7549)\\n\\n### Stabilization of otelgrpc\\n\\n- Community request to stabilize otelgrpc noted by Tyler.\\n\\n- Blockers:\\n\\n  - Stabilization of RPC semantic conventions (semconv) must come first.\\n\\n  - Audit of the current otelgrpc API to remove cruft and confirm stability.\\n\\n- Damien clarified that stabilization does not imply restoring the old interceptor—it should remain removed.\\n\\n- David is willing to drive module stability once semconv stabilizes; however, gRPC engagement has been sporadic and driven by their internal roadmap.\\n\\n- Strategy discussion:\\n\\n  - OTel could continue owning and maintaining a gRPC instrumentation package, with the option to deprecate later if gRPC ships native instrumentation aligned with semconv.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 06 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479655348 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 39 04z updat 2025 11 03t09 40 01z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 30 attende tyler yahn bryan boreham damien mathieu robert paj ą k david ashpol mike blum transcript monitor bug report by os fuzz david propos enabl automat file of os fuzz find a github issu to track and triag them in repo robert note os fuzz run in googl ci access and notif current limit some maintain may need to be ad a contact tyler and david highlight that os fuzz doe not file public issu by default due to potenti secur sensit of fuzz find consensus start by set up a maintain mail list for os fuzz notif via gc and trial monitor for a few month avoid enabl public github issu file for now reassess after triag verif workflow are in place robert can manual recreat older issu if need bryan share prometheus project s recent discuss compar os fuzz with go s built in fuzz robert emphas os fuzz s continu background fuzz a a benefit refer monitor bug report by os fuzz 7549 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 7549 stabil of otelgrpc communiti request to stabil otelgrpc note by tyler blocker stabil of rpc semant convent semconv must come first audit of the current otelgrpc api to remov cruft and confirm stabil damien clarifi that stabil doe not impli restor the old interceptor it should remain remov david is will to drive modul stabil onc semconv stabil howev grpc engag ha been sporad and driven by their intern roadmap strategi discuss otel could continu own and maintain a grpc instrument packag with the option to deprec later if grpc ship nativ instrument align with semconv\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"id\": \"37d8c65557d9108d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32275697623759997, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1538103374822857, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7169658, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 7597, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:24\", \"token_count\": 1926, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"After discussing it at the 23-OCT SIG call, the decision is in the short term to include this in an `init` function in the otelconf package that will automatically configure the SDK components\\n\\n---\\n\\n**dashpole** — 2025-12-04T18:32:17Z\\n\\n> in the short term to include this in an init function in the otelconf package\\n\\nOut of curiosity, what is the long-term plan?\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-05]\\n\\n# Issue: otelconf: add support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE variable (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8059)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8059  \\n\\n**Author**: codeboten  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-22T21:25:29Z · **Updated**: 2026-04-03T11:34:34Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: enhancement, area: file-config  \\n\\n**Milestone**: untracked\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Timeline\\n\\n- 2025-10-22T21:25:30Z · **labeled** by codeboten `enhancement`\\n\\n- 2025-10-22T21:25:42Z · **labeled** by github-actions[bot] `area: file-config`\\n\\n- 2025-10-22T21:27:48Z · **renamed**