annot be used to verify the source code zip file or tarball for a release, since these assets are only created when a download is requested.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src issu 03 issu recommend immut releas open telemetri sig secur 164 canon url http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 author trask creat 2025 08 27t13 31 30z updat 2026 01 28t22 16 50z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label mileston descript http github blog changelog 2025 08 26 releas now support immut in public preview sourc id src issu 03 issu recommend immut releas open telemetri sig secur 164 canon url http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 author trask creat 2025 08 27t13 31 30z updat 2026 01 28t22 16 50z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label mileston discuss 9 pellar 2025 09 16t12 52 39z i test it on my side project check http github com goyek goyek releas tag v2 3 0 and notic the immut text and icon a well a releas attest json in the releas asset test gh releas verifi v2 3 0 repo goyek goyek resolv tag v2 3 0 to sha1 580d400496e680ca42e42e5101f591dc1e6a747c load attest from github api releas v2 3 0 verifi caution it is not possibl to add edit remov releas asset artifact after the releas is publish this is great but mayb some repositori add the asset after the releas is alreadi publish the releas process must be check for the repositori befor enabl the featur import this command can not be use to verifi the sourc code zip file or tarbal for a releas sinc these asset are onli creat when a download is request\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874919b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"id\": \"850c33a1966bb99c\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3106774162376, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1538103374822857, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6767006, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874919b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/sig-security-164.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 6168, \"chunk_count\": 5, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:19\", \"token_count\": 2203, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  - Meeting notes: [Ecosystem Explorer Project](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QBpFmSR54fGus8q6RraUj0-mEjSoX7S7fdlgsvxZsuk/edit?usp=sharing)  \\n\\n  - [https://github.com/mikeblum/otel-explorer-go-docs/blob/3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0/instrumentation-list.yaml](https://github.com/mikeblum/otel-explorer-go-docs/blob/3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0/instrumentation-list.yaml)  \\n\\n### SIG Security: release signing\\n\\n- Robert proposed enabling GitHub “signature releases” in addition to existing tag signing and GPG signatures of source archives.\\n\\n- Key points:\\n\\n  - GitHub’s source tarball/zip is generated at download time; signing artifacts strengthens trust and mitigates changes over time.\\n\\n  - Double-signing is acceptable and beneficial for OSS Scorecard/compliance.\\n\\n  - Constraint: Artifacts must be uploaded at release time; cannot regenerate later.\\n\\n- Decision: Proceed with enabling signature releases; update release documentation and ensure process discipline.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- [https://github.com/open-telemetry/sig-security/issues/164](https://github.com/open-telemetry/sig-security/issues/164)  \\n\\n### KubeCon updates\\n\\n- OpenTelemetry Observatory booth confirmed.\\n\\n- Go SIG will meet at the booth (Tuesday morning, local time; check published schedule).\\n\\n- Plan to cancel the Zoom SIG meeting during KubeCon week; reminder will be sent next week.\\n\\n- Community encouraged to stop by the booth and participate.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-06]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479655348  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:39:04Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:40:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-30\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Bryan Boreham\\n\\n- Damien Mathieu\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"meet note ecosystem explor project http doc googl com document d 1qbpfmsr54fgus8q6rrauj0 mejsox7s7fdlgsvxzsuk edit usp share http github com mikeblum otel explor go doc blob 3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0 instrument list yaml http github com mikeblum otel explor go doc blob 3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0 instrument list yaml sig secur releas sign robert propos enabl github signatur releas in addit to exist tag sign and gpg signatur of sourc archiv key point github s sourc tarbal zip is generat at download time sign artifact strengthen trust and mitig chang over time doubl sign is accept and benefici for os scorecard complianc constraint artifact must be upload at releas time can not regener later decis proceed with enabl signatur releas updat releas document and ensur process disciplin refer http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 kubecon updat opentelemetri observatori booth confirm go sig will meet at the booth tuesday morn local time check publish schedul plan to cancel the zoom sig meet dure kubecon week remind will be sent next week communiti encourag to stop by the booth and particip sourc id src note 06 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479655348 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 39 04z updat 2025 11 03t09 40 01z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 30 attende tyler yahn bryan boreham damien mathieu\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"id\": \"0032f870da180d9a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3074117371442809, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.130529181634687, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7201377, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 7597, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:24\", \"token_count\": 1926, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-05]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479626706  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:30:26Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-23\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Alex Boten\\n\\n- David Ashpole (dashpole)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n### PR status: JSON/YAML unmarshalling\\n\\n- A small change (error tag) was suggested and applied.\\n\\n- Build is running; plan is to merge once green.\\n\\n### Adding env var support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE\\n\\nReference: Adding env var support for OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8059\\n\\n- Goal:\\n\\n  - If the env var is present, load the indicated config file and configure the SDK automatically, minimizing user code.\\n\\n- Current ecosystem notes:\\n\\n  - PHP reports support; other languages vary (JS likely working on it; C++ explicitly not supporting).\\n\\n  - Go users are accustomed to programmatic setup; unclear if SDK-level support is necessary.\\n\\n- Go implementation options discussed:\\n\\n  - SDK experimental feature-flag approach:\\n\\n    - Use internal “x”/experimental packages to expose a feature gate for the env var.\\n\\n    - Check the env var during SDK setup (e.g., TracerProvider construction), and if enabled, configure from the file.\\n\\n    - Complications:\\n\\n      - Potential import cycles (e.g., if otelconf needs sdk and vice versa).\\n\\n      - Decision required on how to handle passed options vs. config file (ignore vs. merge).\\n\\n      - Requires similar work across trace, metrics, and logs modules.\\n\\n  - Contrib-first approach (preferred short term):\\n\\n    - Implement in opentelemetry-go-contrib/otelconf:\\n\\n      - Provide an explicit function to load from OTEL_EXPERIMENTAL_CONFIG_FILE and construct/return SDK providers.\\n\\n      - Optionally offer an init-based side effect that sets the global provider if the env var is set (not ideal, but acceptable during experimental phase to collect feedback).\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 05 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479626706 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z updat 2025 11 03t09 30 26z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 23 attende tyler yahn alex boten david ashpol dashpol transcript pr status json yaml unmarshal a small chang error tag wa suggest and appli build is run plan is to merg onc green ad env var support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file refer ad env var support for otel _ experiment _ config _ file http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8059 goal if the env var is present load the indic config file and configur the sdk automat minim user code current ecosystem note php report support other languag vari j like work on it c explicit not support go user are accustom to programmat setup unclear if sdk level support is necessari go implement option discuss sdk experiment featur flag approach use intern x experiment packag to expos a featur gate for the env var check the env var dure sdk setup e g tracerprovid construct and if enabl configur from the file complic potenti import cycl e g if otelconf need sdk and vice versa decis requir on how to handl pass option v config file ignor v merg requir similar work across trace metric and log modul contrib first approach prefer short term implement in opentelemetri go contrib otelconf provid an explicit function to load from otel _ experiment _ config _ file and construct return sdk provid option offer an init base side effect that set the global provid if the env var is set not ideal but accept dure experiment phase to collect feedback\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"873abbfe8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"id\": \"1fe86388dce9138e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30703499714428084, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.130529181634687, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7188819, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"873abbfe8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 4412, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"creat